  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1035 PM CDT Sun Jun 28 2026\n\nThere will be no appreciable abatement in the heat and humidity\nthroughout the 7-day forecast. Temperatures and heat indices may\nback off slightly by the weekend, but additional heat advisories\nmay still be needed. Look for mainly low rain and storm chances to\ndevelop later this week, owing primarily to instability generated\nby surface heating. There are slightly better rain and storm\nchances next weekend, possibly owing to an upper trough passage,\nbut QPF totals from Monday through next Sunday night are below\n1/2\" for all of Middle Tennessee except for some parts of the\nCumberland Plateau. Indeed, the primary focus with this forecast \nis the heat. No other hazardous weather is anticipated at this \ntime.",
